WEBVTT

00:03.462 --> 00:05.630
¶ men. ¶

00:22.181 --> 00:23.915
(rattling)

00:38.564 --> 00:41.366
Oh, dear!

00:41.367 --> 00:42.801
(gasps)

00:42.802 --> 00:45.437
I'm sorry, did
I wake you up?

00:45.438 --> 00:46.871
What are you doing?

00:46.872 --> 00:51.242
I was trying to find
a nice way to wake you up.

00:51.243 --> 00:53.344
Well, kudos, you found one.

00:53.345 --> 00:56.614
Here. Merry day
before christmas.

00:56.615 --> 00:58.950
I thought we agreed not
to exchange presents.

00:58.951 --> 01:02.520
Well, you gave me a pretty
nice present last night.

01:02.521 --> 01:03.888
Actually two.

01:03.889 --> 01:06.224
You're terrible.

01:06.225 --> 01:07.692
Open it.

01:12.064 --> 01:16.768
Dare I say it?
Key to your heart?

01:16.769 --> 01:18.703
Better. It's a key
to my house.

01:18.704 --> 01:22.774
Walden, I can't accept
a key to your house.

01:22.775 --> 01:24.943
It's a bit premature.

01:24.944 --> 01:27.245
Well, if anything in our
relationship's going
to be premature,

01:27.246 --> 01:29.113
I prefer it to be
the house key.

01:29.114 --> 01:32.517
It's a very sweet gesture.

01:34.553 --> 01:35.920
Mistletoe.

01:37.623 --> 01:38.923
Oh, my!

01:38.924 --> 01:41.125
I've got to pick up my daughter
from her father's

01:41.126 --> 01:43.962
And I've got to get to the
airport to pick up my parents.

01:43.963 --> 01:45.797
Are you sure I can't
come with you?

01:45.798 --> 01:46.831
Positive.

01:46.832 --> 01:48.900
Why not?
We get along great.

01:48.901 --> 01:51.302
Your parents are in town,
my mom's coming to visit.

01:51.303 --> 01:52.604
It's christmas.

01:52.605 --> 01:55.073
What better time for everybody
to get to know each other?

01:55.074 --> 01:57.575
Walden, we're still
getting to know each other.

01:57.576 --> 02:00.111
I know you.
Really?

02:00.112 --> 02:02.313
What color
are my eyes then?

02:02.314 --> 02:04.849
Brown. The left one's got a
little fleck of green in it.

02:04.850 --> 02:06.951
Damn.

02:06.952 --> 02:11.122
You say you're a size two,
but you're actually a size four.

02:11.123 --> 02:12.724
You run the water
in the bathroom

02:12.725 --> 02:16.261
To cover the sound
of you peeing.

02:16.262 --> 02:19.397
All right fine. Let me put it
another way.

02:19.398 --> 02:21.199
No families this year.

02:21.200 --> 02:24.335
And I am a size two.

02:25.170 --> 02:27.105
Merry christmas.

02:27.907 --> 02:30.241
She took the key.

02:32.778 --> 02:35.246
Aw!

02:35.247 --> 02:37.949
¶ men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ¶

02:43.997 --> 02:46.031
¶ men. ¶

02:46.032 --> 02:46.999
(berta sighs)

02:47.000 --> 02:48.701
When's your mom
getting in?

02:48.702 --> 02:50.035
Any time now.

02:50.036 --> 02:51.570
She's on her way
up from san diego.

02:51.571 --> 02:53.572
Oh, hey, is jake's room ready?

02:53.573 --> 02:54.907
I did what I could.

02:54.908 --> 02:57.276
It still has kind of
a teenage stink to it.

02:57.277 --> 03:00.146
Maybe I should put her
in alan's room.

03:00.147 --> 03:02.782
Oh, no, that smells
like failure and foot powder.

03:03.984 --> 03:05.918
Is that mistletoe?

03:05.919 --> 03:06.986
Yes.

03:06.987 --> 03:08.721
Well, bring it, santa.

03:09.990 --> 03:12.825
Oh, merry christmas to me.

03:12.826 --> 03:16.429
You know they make belt
buckles with mistletoe on 'em?

03:16.430 --> 03:17.930
You're kidding.

03:17.931 --> 03:19.165
Check your stocking.

03:19.166 --> 03:21.200
(chuckles)

03:21.201 --> 03:24.537
So, listen, uh, I want to give
you a nice christmas bonus.

03:24.538 --> 03:26.238
What do you think
would make you happy?

03:26.239 --> 03:29.341
Check your damn stocking
and put on the buckle.

03:30.844 --> 03:33.679
How about three weeks pay and
another kiss on the cheek?

03:33.680 --> 03:35.347
Do I get to pick
the cheek?

03:36.683 --> 03:38.851
Merry christmas.

03:39.719 --> 03:42.321
Merry christmas.

03:42.322 --> 03:45.591
(ringtone playing)

03:47.461 --> 03:50.796
Hey, mom, where are you?

03:51.765 --> 03:55.267
Oh, okay,
that's about ten miles away...

03:55.268 --> 03:58.804
And it's rush hour,
so figure... Three hours.

03:59.606 --> 04:02.274
Yeah, I can't wait
to see you, too.

04:02.275 --> 04:04.310
So I'm thinking that since

04:04.311 --> 04:06.312
This is our first christmas
without charlie,

04:06.313 --> 04:07.746
We should spend it together.

04:07.747 --> 04:12.084
Yes, mom,
I'd rather get laid, too...

04:12.085 --> 04:14.520
But I think
family is more important.

04:14.521 --> 04:15.788
Hey, mom.

04:15.789 --> 04:18.357
Yeah, I'm just driving
to dad's.

04:18.358 --> 04:23.095
In 500 feet,
turn left.

04:23.096 --> 04:26.599
Yes, I'm seeing someone.

04:26.600 --> 04:28.567
No, you can't meet her.

04:28.568 --> 04:31.170
Because it's too soon.

04:31.171 --> 04:32.338
I don't know what it means.

04:32.339 --> 04:34.340
It's just
what she keeps telling me.

04:34.341 --> 04:35.841
Uh, mom, y-you're breaking up.

04:35.842 --> 04:38.043
I-I'm sorry, what did you say?

04:38.879 --> 04:42.047
Y-y-you want a tuna sandwich?

04:42.048 --> 04:46.285
Oh, oh, you're
in a two-man sandwich.

04:46.286 --> 04:51.223
Uh, well, I, I hope
they're using condiments.

04:51.224 --> 04:54.393
Uh, well, listen, I-I-I got
to go, I got another call.

04:54.394 --> 04:56.228
Dear lord.

04:56.229 --> 04:57.596
Hello.

04:57.597 --> 04:59.498
Oh, jake, merry christmas.

04:59.499 --> 05:00.766
Hey, dad,
I just wanted to call

05:00.767 --> 05:03.335
And tell you merry christmas
and wish you happy holidays.

05:03.336 --> 05:05.304
No, no, mom and herb
are out to dinner.

05:05.305 --> 05:08.073
I'm just chilling
at the ski lodge.

05:08.074 --> 05:09.742
Room service.

05:09.743 --> 05:10.876
Oh, hang on.

05:10.877 --> 05:11.911
I ordered
a cheeseburger.

05:11.912 --> 05:13.112
Got to go, dad.

05:13.113 --> 05:14.914
Yeah, I know
the tip's included.

05:14.915 --> 05:16.715
All right, bye.

05:16.716 --> 05:17.716
All right, now you call your mom

05:17.717 --> 05:19.618
And tell her
you're with your dad.

05:22.956 --> 05:26.825
Hey, mom, I'm with your dad.

05:26.826 --> 05:27.927
No, no.

05:29.729 --> 05:31.764
¶ men. ¶

05:31.765 --> 05:33.799
This is gonna be
the best christmas ever.

05:33.800 --> 05:35.534
Yeah, swell.

05:35.535 --> 05:37.169
I got a great
new girlfriend.

05:37.170 --> 05:40.706
My girlfriend's got a
great new boyfriend.

05:40.707 --> 05:42.641
My mom is coming.

05:42.642 --> 05:45.811
So is mine.

05:47.681 --> 05:50.816
Wherever she is.

05:50.817 --> 05:52.051
Went to the apple store

05:52.052 --> 05:54.253
And bought myself
a bunch of cool presents.

05:54.254 --> 05:57.656
I went to the grocery store
and got myself an apple.

05:59.392 --> 06:02.595
Sounds like somebody's got
the holiday blues.

06:02.596 --> 06:03.762
Oh, little bit.

06:03.763 --> 06:05.598
My son's with his
mother and her husband,

06:05.599 --> 06:07.833
And this is my first christmas
without charlie.

06:07.834 --> 06:09.501
What would you two
normally do?

06:09.502 --> 06:11.503
Oh, we had kind of
a holiday tradition.

06:11.504 --> 06:14.039
Um, he would drink
a gallon of eggnog

06:14.040 --> 06:16.875
And then try to throw me
out of the house at gunpoint.

06:16.876 --> 06:19.078
Good times.

06:20.180 --> 06:22.414
Well, you're not going
to spend this year alone.

06:22.415 --> 06:25.017
You're going to have christmas
with me and my mom.

06:25.018 --> 06:26.919
Well, thank you,
that's very nice of you.

06:26.920 --> 06:28.520
You want to hear a funny idea?

06:28.521 --> 06:30.189
You and my mom
are about the same age.

06:30.190 --> 06:32.291
If you guys started dating
and got married,

06:32.292 --> 06:34.259
You'd be my new daddy.

06:34.260 --> 06:37.329
Wait, h-hold on,
I-I'm your mom's age?

06:37.330 --> 06:38.931
How old do you think I am?

06:38.932 --> 06:41.367
I don't know, what, like 60?

06:41.368 --> 06:43.969
I'm 44.

06:43.970 --> 06:45.871
Oh, well, you look older.

06:45.872 --> 06:47.873
(doorbell rings)

06:47.874 --> 06:49.842
Oh, there she is.

06:49.843 --> 06:50.843
That's it.

06:50.844 --> 06:53.312
Tomorrow I start moisturizing.

06:54.347 --> 06:56.915
Mom.
Baby.

06:57.951 --> 06:59.518
(sighs)
eyeball, eyeball.

06:59.519 --> 07:01.153
Nose and mouth.

07:01.154 --> 07:02.187
I love you north.

07:02.188 --> 07:03.155
I love you south.

07:03.156 --> 07:04.323
(both laugh)

07:04.324 --> 07:05.424
(sighs)

07:05.425 --> 07:07.426
Hey, alan, meet
my mother robin.

07:07.427 --> 07:08.727
Nice to meet you, alan.

07:08.728 --> 07:09.862
Likewise.

07:09.863 --> 07:11.530
Mom, let me show
you my place.

07:11.531 --> 07:14.299
Check it out, I
got my own ocean.

07:14.300 --> 07:15.868
Well, it's not
completely mine.

07:15.869 --> 07:17.903
I have to share the
other side with japan.

07:17.904 --> 07:19.505
It's very nice, dear.

07:19.506 --> 07:21.840
Walden:
Yeah, I'm rich.

07:21.841 --> 07:26.111
Well... I know
what I want for christmas.

07:26.913 --> 07:29.548
¶ men. ¶

07:29.549 --> 07:32.251
So how long have you two
been living together?

07:32.252 --> 07:34.486
A couple
of months.

07:34.487 --> 07:37.089
I see.

07:37.090 --> 07:39.024
I'm sorry, I-I have to ask.

07:39.025 --> 07:41.393
Is this the woman
you don't want me to meet?

07:43.096 --> 07:44.930
What?

07:44.931 --> 07:45.964
No.

07:45.965 --> 07:47.366
No, alan is just a friend.

07:47.367 --> 07:48.567
Tell her.

07:48.568 --> 07:51.637
&lt;i>Butch and sundance,&lt;/i>
not &lt;i>brokeback mountain.&lt;/i>

07:51.638 --> 07:53.305
Okay, sorry.

07:53.306 --> 07:55.607
I-I mean, you have to admit,
it's a rather strange set-up--

07:55.608 --> 07:59.111
A 33-year-old man living
with a 60-year-old.

08:00.480 --> 08:02.481
I'm 44.

08:02.482 --> 08:04.483
Right, me, too.

08:06.086 --> 08:07.753
Alan helped me through
my break-up with bridget,

08:07.754 --> 08:09.088
And then he needed
a place to stay,

08:09.089 --> 08:11.156
So I asked him
to stick around.

08:11.157 --> 08:13.158
Oh, that is so like you.

08:13.159 --> 08:14.193
(walden and robin chuckle)

08:14.194 --> 08:15.961
When walden was
a little boy,

08:15.962 --> 08:19.631
He used to bring home sick,
helpless animals all the time.

08:21.434 --> 08:24.937
God help me,
I can't take that as an insult.

08:24.938 --> 08:27.005
So, uh, what do you do, robin?

08:27.006 --> 08:27.940
I'm a primatologist.

08:27.941 --> 08:29.842
I, I work mainly
with gorillas.

08:29.843 --> 08:33.645
Oh, oh, so I guess that makes
you the gorilla my dreams.

08:33.646 --> 08:35.514
(laughing)

08:37.317 --> 08:39.485
It was hysterical
when bugs bunny did it.

08:40.286 --> 08:42.421
And thanks
to the financial support

08:42.422 --> 08:43.789
Of my brilliant son,
I have a private

08:43.790 --> 08:45.491
Gorilla sanctuary in temecula.

08:45.492 --> 08:46.258
Oh, no kidding?

08:46.259 --> 08:47.392
Yeah, we take
gorillas

08:47.393 --> 08:48.560
Who were born
in captivity

08:48.561 --> 08:50.295
And those who have lost
their wild habitats

08:50.296 --> 08:52.197
And provide them
with a safe, stable,

08:52.198 --> 08:53.866
Loving family
environment.

08:53.867 --> 08:55.868
Oh, that sounds wonderful.

08:55.869 --> 08:59.138
Does one have to be a gorilla
to apply for admittance?

08:59.139 --> 09:00.439
I'm afraid so.

09:00.440 --> 09:02.407
Story of my life.

09:02.408 --> 09:03.575
When I was little,
I always wanted

09:03.576 --> 09:04.777
To play with the gorillas.

09:04.778 --> 09:07.646
I even made up my own
imaginary gorilla friend.

09:07.647 --> 09:09.014
Remember magilla, mom?

09:09.015 --> 09:11.717
Hmm, yeah,
but he wasn't imaginary.

09:11.718 --> 09:13.685
What?

09:13.686 --> 09:15.387
Walden, magilla lived
with us

09:15.388 --> 09:17.623
For the first four years
of your life.

09:18.458 --> 09:20.025
He was real?

09:21.361 --> 09:22.461
Yeah.

09:22.462 --> 09:23.896
Do you want
to see some pictures?

09:23.897 --> 09:28.066
Wait, w-w-wait,
magilla was real?

09:28.067 --> 09:29.501
Very much so.

09:29.502 --> 09:31.637
Wait, you actually had
a gorilla living with you?

09:31.638 --> 09:34.773
Yep, I was doing experiments
to see if gorillas could learn

09:34.774 --> 09:36.308
As fast as human children, so

09:36.309 --> 09:38.844
I raised magilla and walden
together from birth.

09:38.845 --> 09:40.879
Wow.

09:40.880 --> 09:44.316
All we had was a schnauzer
and an argentinean tennis pro.

09:46.152 --> 09:49.321
Uncle javier.

09:50.223 --> 09:52.691
The tennis pro,
not the schnauzer.

09:52.692 --> 09:57.095
Hold on a second,
I was raised with a gorilla?

09:57.096 --> 09:59.731
Oh, well, just until
you started preschool.

09:59.732 --> 10:03.235
Now, look, here's you and
magilla together in your crib.

10:07.340 --> 10:08.574
And here's

10:08.575 --> 10:11.043
The two of you
at your first birthday.

10:12.078 --> 10:13.979
Wait a minute,

10:13.980 --> 10:16.782
Is that how I learned
sign language?

10:16.783 --> 10:19.084
I'm sorry, I don't have
any bananas.

10:19.085 --> 10:20.953
Look, there's
the two of you

10:20.954 --> 10:23.455
On the playground.

10:23.456 --> 10:24.723
Oh, your first
Halloween.

10:25.558 --> 10:27.593
You went as a gorilla,

10:27.594 --> 10:29.027
And magilla went as a ghost.

10:32.031 --> 10:33.999
Walden:
Whoa, whoa.

10:34.000 --> 10:36.668
Yeah, okay. Yeah, it's
starting to come back to me.

10:36.669 --> 10:37.903
Like, riding
tricycles together,

10:37.904 --> 10:40.138
And running...
Running around the house.

10:40.139 --> 10:42.708
Or playing hide in the closet.

10:42.709 --> 10:45.577
Wait. Why were we always
hiding in the closet?

10:45.578 --> 10:48.447
Well, the homeowners association
didn't allow cats or dogs.

10:48.448 --> 10:50.716
What would they have said
about a gorilla?

10:50.717 --> 10:52.718
Yeah. I remember.

10:52.719 --> 10:54.620
You told me he was my brother.

10:54.621 --> 10:56.955
Well, in a sense, he was.

10:56.956 --> 10:59.124
And then one day, he was gone.

10:59.125 --> 11:01.159
Yeah.

11:01.160 --> 11:03.262
You said
he got sent back to the jungle.

11:03.263 --> 11:04.997
Well, sweetheart,
we didn't have any choice.

11:04.998 --> 11:06.732
He was getting too big.
He, uh...

11:06.733 --> 11:09.001
He tried
to kill a jehovah's witness.

11:10.904 --> 11:13.338
Now, now, to be fair,
who among us hasn't...

11:13.339 --> 11:14.606
Not now, alan.

11:16.342 --> 11:18.277
This is really starting
to freak me out.

11:18.278 --> 11:19.444
Well, sweetie,
I-I don't understand

11:19.445 --> 11:21.780
Why you're making such
a big deal out of this.

11:21.781 --> 11:23.715
You're kidding, right?

11:23.716 --> 11:27.052
I-I just discovered
that my brother is a gorilla!

11:27.053 --> 11:29.421
That's-that's
kind of a big deal!

11:29.422 --> 11:31.123
Hey, my brother was a pig,
so, I mean...

11:31.124 --> 11:33.358
I said, not now, alan!

11:34.427 --> 11:36.328
Walden, calm down.

11:36.329 --> 11:39.531
You do realize
that I spent my entire childhood

11:39.532 --> 11:40.899
Worrying that if I misbehaved,

11:40.900 --> 11:43.602
I would get sent away
to the jungle like magilla!

11:43.603 --> 11:46.204
One false move, zimbabwe!

11:46.205 --> 11:48.206
Well, sweetheart, I...

11:48.207 --> 11:50.409
I never knew
that you felt like that.

11:50.410 --> 11:51.710
Of course you didn't.

11:51.711 --> 11:54.112
You were so busy
doing your experiment!

11:54.981 --> 11:57.082
Walden!

11:57.083 --> 11:58.951
(door closes)

11:58.952 --> 12:01.119
Kids, huh?

12:01.120 --> 12:02.521
So, you seeing anybody?

12:06.809 --> 12:08.543
¶ men. ¶

12:08.544 --> 12:10.712
Walden, it's mom.
Where are you?

12:10.713 --> 12:13.314
Please call me back
so we can talk about this.

12:13.315 --> 12:17.685
I had no idea he'd repressed
all those childhood memories.

12:17.686 --> 12:19.054
Well, apparently,

12:19.055 --> 12:21.456
Losing what he thought was
his sibling was very traumatic.

12:21.457 --> 12:24.893
I'm wondering if maybe I have
to rethink his christmas gift.

12:24.894 --> 12:26.628
Why? What did you get him?

12:26.629 --> 12:29.130
A bathrobe.

12:29.131 --> 12:30.899
Yeah, not a good idea.

12:30.900 --> 12:32.634
And I can't even return it.

12:32.635 --> 12:35.303
It's slightly irregular.

12:35.304 --> 12:37.806
You must think
I'm a terrible mother.

12:37.807 --> 12:41.476
Well, let's compare
mothering techniques.

12:41.477 --> 12:43.545
Um, did you tell him
that disneyland burned down

12:43.546 --> 12:45.113
To avoid having
to take him there

12:45.114 --> 12:46.748
For his sixth, seventh
and eighth birthdays?

12:46.749 --> 12:47.949
No.

12:47.950 --> 12:49.651
Did you tell him
to walk it off

12:49.652 --> 12:50.819
After his appendix burst?

12:50.820 --> 12:52.487
No.

12:52.488 --> 12:54.522
Did you tell me
the only reason you got pregnant

12:54.523 --> 12:56.391
Was because you didn't want
to smear your lipstick?

12:56.392 --> 12:59.694
Of course not!

12:59.695 --> 13:01.262
Then, far as I'm concerned,

13:01.263 --> 13:03.832
You're mother
of the freakin' year. Hmm.

13:03.833 --> 13:05.800
Mm. Although I did store
walden's embryo

13:05.801 --> 13:08.236
In a cryogenic chamber until
magilla's mother got pregnant

13:08.237 --> 13:10.672
So they could be born
at the same time.

13:10.673 --> 13:13.441
Okay, flag on the play.

13:13.442 --> 13:14.976
You did what?

13:14.977 --> 13:17.045
I needed my child
and the gorilla

13:17.046 --> 13:19.747
To be born at the same time
for the experiment to be valid.

13:19.748 --> 13:21.549
And your husband
was okay with this?

13:21.550 --> 13:23.651
It was for science.

13:23.652 --> 13:25.854
And I may not have told him.

13:25.855 --> 13:28.990
Okay, well, well, after all
that time and energy,

13:28.991 --> 13:30.425
What did you learn?

13:30.426 --> 13:33.394
My son is smarter
than a gorilla.

13:33.395 --> 13:36.364
Mine's not.

13:36.365 --> 13:39.901
¶ men. ¶

13:46.509 --> 13:48.576
Oh, walden,
what are you doing here?

13:48.577 --> 13:51.379
My brother is a gorilla,
and she sent him away.

13:51.380 --> 13:55.350
I'm sorry. Is that some sort
of american &lt;i>christmas carol?&lt;/i>

13:55.351 --> 13:57.519
No. It's a succinct summation

13:57.520 --> 14:00.955
Of my seminal years
with a simian sibling.

14:00.956 --> 14:03.124
Are you drunk?

14:03.125 --> 14:05.760
I ought to be.
I've taken the necessary steps.

14:06.862 --> 14:08.997
(whispering):
Sweetie, this isn't
a very good time.

14:08.998 --> 14:10.365
You're telling me.

14:10.366 --> 14:11.966
My mother is a mad scientist,

14:11.967 --> 14:14.502
And I spent the first four years
of my life

14:14.503 --> 14:17.705
Flinging poop with my brother...
The gorilla.

14:17.706 --> 14:19.841
Hello!

14:19.842 --> 14:21.709
Mummy and daddy,

14:21.710 --> 14:24.112
This is the fellow
I was telling you about.

14:24.113 --> 14:25.380
How do you do?

14:25.381 --> 14:28.583
Wing commander edward
hyde-tottingham, r.A.F. Retired.

14:28.584 --> 14:30.218
This is my wife sharon.

14:30.219 --> 14:31.486
Hello.

14:31.487 --> 14:32.854
Nice to meet you.

14:32.855 --> 14:34.389
Let me ask you something, shary.

14:35.824 --> 14:37.458
Would you have raised
your daughter

14:37.459 --> 14:39.260
With a jungle beast
in an effort

14:39.261 --> 14:41.796
To satisfy
your scientific curiosity?

14:41.797 --> 14:46.000
Well... I really couldn't say.

14:46.001 --> 14:49.504
I have cross-bred orchids.

14:49.505 --> 14:50.538
Yes. They're lovely.

14:50.539 --> 14:51.973
(chuckles)

14:51.974 --> 14:53.775
As are you, my darling.

14:53.776 --> 14:55.643
(stammering):
Walden, I don't understand.

14:55.644 --> 14:57.478
Did something happen
with your mother?

14:57.479 --> 14:59.013
Oh, yeah, something happened.

14:59.014 --> 15:01.316
My entire life is a lie.

15:01.317 --> 15:04.886
You know why I try so hard
to please you sexually?

15:04.887 --> 15:06.454
Because

15:06.455 --> 15:08.957
I'm afraid if I don't
give you multiple orgasms,

15:08.958 --> 15:14.162
That you'll banish
me to central africa.

15:14.163 --> 15:16.364
What?!
(clears throat)

15:16.365 --> 15:21.135
The commander and I have often
traveled to africa on safari.

15:21.136 --> 15:22.537
Is that so?

15:22.538 --> 15:24.038
Oh, yes.

15:24.039 --> 15:27.575
Though I can't say
I've ever had multiple orgasms.

15:29.011 --> 15:31.179
Lucky if I get the one.

15:35.284 --> 15:38.253
¶ men. ¶

15:38.254 --> 15:40.321
Come on, walden,
call me back.

15:40.322 --> 15:42.490
I'm worried sick.

15:42.491 --> 15:45.560
He always disappears
like this when he's upset.

15:45.561 --> 15:48.029
As a child, he'd climb
into a tree to sulk,

15:48.030 --> 15:49.831
And when I'd try
to get him down,

15:49.832 --> 15:51.799
He'd beat his chest
and bellow at me.

15:51.800 --> 15:53.735
Remind you of anybody?

15:53.736 --> 15:56.671
Yeah. His father.

15:56.672 --> 15:59.073
(phone ringing)

15:59.074 --> 16:01.075
Hello?

16:01.076 --> 16:02.343
Oh, uh, hi, zoey.

16:02.344 --> 16:05.146
Walden's not here.

16:05.147 --> 16:06.381
Really?

16:06.382 --> 16:09.083
Okay, well, well, thanks
for letting me know.

16:09.084 --> 16:10.318
What's going on?

16:10.319 --> 16:12.320
Apparently, your son got drunk

16:12.321 --> 16:14.155
And climbed up
onto his girlfriend's roof.

16:14.156 --> 16:15.189
He, what?

16:15.190 --> 16:16.824
Still early. We could
catch a movie.

16:16.825 --> 16:19.227
Are you out of your mind?
We have to go get him.

16:19.228 --> 16:21.929
Oh, oh, absolutely, sure. I was
just about to suggest that.

16:21.930 --> 16:23.431
Are you on facebook?

16:23.432 --> 16:25.633
Maybe I could give
you a poke sometime.

16:25.634 --> 16:29.137
¶ men. ¶

16:37.546 --> 16:39.314
(sighs)

16:39.315 --> 16:42.016
Uh... Walden?

16:42.017 --> 16:43.418
What are you doing here?

16:43.419 --> 16:45.453
(grunting)

16:45.454 --> 16:48.289
Well... To be perfectly honest,

16:48.290 --> 16:51.526
I'm trying
to impress your mother.

16:51.527 --> 16:54.195
Why? She used me
as a guinea pig.

16:54.196 --> 16:56.030
Yeah, well,
my mother once left me

16:56.031 --> 16:57.765
At summer camp
till thanksgiving.

16:57.766 --> 16:59.600
So?

16:59.601 --> 17:02.036
So, we can't keep
blaming our parents

17:02.037 --> 17:03.738
For how our lives turned out.

17:03.739 --> 17:05.907
Oh! Oh!

17:08.043 --> 17:09.210
(debris clattering)

17:09.211 --> 17:10.978
Be careful.
If you fall, you'll die.

17:10.979 --> 17:14.115
Thank you.

17:14.116 --> 17:15.783
Did you forgive your mother?

17:15.784 --> 17:18.119
No, never,

17:18.120 --> 17:20.421
But I'm a small, petty man.

17:20.422 --> 17:23.124
You, however,
have accomplished great things

17:23.125 --> 17:26.561
And have the capacity
to accomplish even more.

17:26.562 --> 17:28.563
What about magilla?

17:28.564 --> 17:31.632
I loved him,
and she just sent him away.

17:31.633 --> 17:34.502
Yeah. That's rough.

17:34.503 --> 17:37.638
But I know what it's like
to lose a brother.

17:38.941 --> 17:42.343
Who, by the way, also tried
to kill a jehovah's witness.

17:43.512 --> 17:44.779
He was hung over,

17:44.780 --> 17:46.948
And they just kept ringing
that damn doorbell.

17:46.949 --> 17:48.950
(helicopter whirring)

17:48.951 --> 17:51.085
Man (through p.A.):
This is the lapd.

17:51.086 --> 17:53.321
Please get off of the roof!

17:54.823 --> 17:56.357
Go away! Leave me alone!

17:56.358 --> 17:58.626
Don't wave your arms
at the aircraft.

17:58.627 --> 18:00.895
That never ends well.

18:03.065 --> 18:04.699
Get out of here!

18:04.700 --> 18:06.033
It's all right!

18:06.034 --> 18:09.203
It's just a mother issue!

18:09.204 --> 18:13.174
Walden, you come down
from there right now!

18:13.175 --> 18:14.876
Oh, excuse me?

18:14.877 --> 18:16.544
Are you walden's mum?

18:16.545 --> 18:18.579
Yes. Are-are you zoey?

18:18.580 --> 18:20.982
I am.
It's so nice
to meet you.

18:20.983 --> 18:22.617
Likewise. These
are my parents.

18:22.618 --> 18:25.086
Wing commander
edward hyde-tottingham.

18:25.087 --> 18:26.354
This is my
wife sharon.

18:26.355 --> 18:27.722
Lovely to meet you.

18:27.723 --> 18:29.657
(walden bellowing)

18:29.658 --> 18:31.592
Your son's
a charming
young man.

18:31.593 --> 18:33.928
Yes, charming.

18:33.929 --> 18:35.196
Thank you.

18:35.197 --> 18:38.132
Thinks he's
the brother
of a monkey.

18:38.133 --> 18:40.101
What's all that about?

18:40.102 --> 18:42.303
(walden bellowing)

18:49.978 --> 18:52.346
I think
that's my dad up there.

18:52.347 --> 18:54.849
I think you're right.

18:54.850 --> 18:56.717
Want to get some
frozen yogurt?

18:56.718 --> 18:58.386
Totally.

18:58.387 --> 19:00.621
¶ men. ¶

19:05.394 --> 19:06.761
¶ men. ¶

19:06.762 --> 19:08.629
Walden, I hope
you understand, honey,

19:08.630 --> 19:10.765
I never meant to hurt you.

19:10.766 --> 19:12.833
I know.

19:12.834 --> 19:14.969
This is the best
christmas gift ever.

19:14.970 --> 19:16.771
Oh, I'm so glad.

19:19.408 --> 19:21.842
(sighs)

19:21.843 --> 19:24.278
See you in a few.

19:29.918 --> 19:32.019
You really are
a terrific mom.

19:32.020 --> 19:33.854
Oh, thanks.

19:33.855 --> 19:35.523
And woman.

19:35.524 --> 19:37.792
Give it a rest, alan.

19:39.895 --> 19:42.230
(snorting)

19:44.700 --> 19:46.901
(chuffing)

19:47.736 --> 19:49.036
Magilla?

19:49.037 --> 19:51.806
(snorting)

19:54.876 --> 19:57.078
(vocalizing)

20:06.755 --> 20:09.590
(vocalizing)

20:30.112 --> 20:32.913
That's the most beautiful
thing I've ever seen.

20:32.914 --> 20:35.049
Yeah.

20:35.050 --> 20:37.285
What's the taser for?

20:37.286 --> 20:40.288
That's a 400-pound gorilla.

20:40.289 --> 20:43.958
This really could have
gone either way.

20:43.959 --> 20:48.029
